  "text": "Hold something firmly in place, or keep it safe.\n\nA place where flowers or other plants are grown.\n\nMara’s lantern shows the gift repaired together.\n\nA fastening made by looping and tightening rope.\n\nFeel sad because someone or something is absent.\n\nPip and Grandma plant the lantern seed together.\n\nHear Grandma and Mara finish their conversation.\n\nExtending a large distance or lasting much time.\n\nWant or enjoy; sometimes used to compare things.\n\nInformation you want to tell or send to someone.\n\nSol shared this draft. Its ending is still open.\n\nSaid something to get an answer or request help.\n\nBring Pip beside the seed boat to load the seed.\n\nStay until something happens or someone arrives.\n\nPutting things into a chosen order or position.\n\nWater entering through a hole or damaged place.\n\nBelonging specifically to the person mentioned.\n\nLarge bags used for carrying or storing things.\n\nNot including the person or thing that follows.\n\nPut something more with what was already there.\n\nYou steer the seed boat · Pip waits on the bank\n\nFollowing the length or direction of something.\n\nPip waits at the dock while Mara does her work.\n\nClick a word for its meaning and pronunciation.\n\nSol shared his draft. Its ending is still open.\n\nPeople travelling in a vehicle, such as a boat.\n\nCooked food using dry heat, usually in an oven.\n\nSomething you have said you will definitely do.\n\nThe two edges of the river in this instruction.\n\nThe place where the small boat starts its trip.\n\nFeedback stopped. Your recording is still here.\n\nThe path used to get from one place to another.\n\nHear Grandma’s offer to send her story to Mara.\n\nA fine powder made from grain, used for baking.\n\nFastenings made by looping and tightening rope.\n\nCarry out an action; also helps form questions.",
  "textSha256": "61d440328993aed04c8dfdfeba72a08912c092afb85a71db70a7df8efa3d2773",
